          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തണൽ — taṇal — \"shade\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉച്ചയ്ക്ക് ഞങ്ങൾ ഒരു വലിയ മരത്തിന്റെ തണലിൽ ഇരുന്നു. uccaykkŭ ñaṅṅaḷ oru valiya marattinṟe taṇalil irunnu. At noon we sat in the shade of a big tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Shade is a kind of coolness: the word comes from the same root as തണുപ്പ്."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തണൽ (taṇal) is native Dravidian, from the root of തണുപ്പ്, cold; DEDR lists it as shade, a shady spot (DEDR 3045)."
            }
          ]
        },
